  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nA cold front that has moved through west central Ohio will continue\nsoutheast across the region through the evening into the early\novernight. A fairly solid line of showers with a bit of embedded\nthunder has developed along the front with isolated convection also\noccurring well ahead of the boundary. There is still a reasonable\namount of CAPE available, but lapse rates have become rather\nunimpressive. So cannot rule out a stronger cell, but overall the\nthreat is low. Expect all activity to weaken as it gets further into\nthe diurnal cooling cycle.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nHigh pressure will build into the region behind the front for mid \nweek. Calmer/drier/cooler weather is expected into the late week. \nTemperatures will then begin to slowly moderate toward more \nseasonable values as we head into the weekend.",
